 "result": "This is expected behavior, and the docs say so. Look at two places:\n\n- **`docs/errorhandling.rst` (~lines 166–173):** \"the bundle cannot handle 404 routing errors because the 404 occurs at the routing level before the bundle can be determined.\" For an unknown URL no route matches, so no bundle is associated with the request. Only app-level handlers are consulted.\n- **`src/tessel/app.py` and `src/tessel/sansio/`:** check the exception handler lookup, which should be `_find_error_handler` or similar. It picks handlers by `request.bundle` (or the bundle names derived from it), and that is `None` for routing failures. This is where you can confirm the behavior.\n\n**Fix:** register the 404 handler on the app instead (`@app.fault_handler(404)`, per the docs' naming here). If you need per-bundle output, branch inside that app-level handler on `request.path` prefix.\n\nI haven't opened `app.py` or `sansio/` yet, so the handler-lookup part is inferred from the docs.",
